{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04E1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-closed-immersions}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d3fbade8c21a157f5e10072390a75b5b4898e122cefd2440922d1dc11f747c39", "source_text": "Closed immersions and pushforward", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bb2db24d6263c73bb2bae8bed28cc6d4882fb62ea11fd7c8a138641385f4cf38", "unit_id": "tag:04E1:title"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04E1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\Sch/X \\longrightarrow \\Sch/Z, \\quad\nU \\longmapsto U_Z = Z \\times_X U\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\mapsto U_Z$", "MATH_0004": "$U_Z$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{proposition-closed-immersion-pushforward}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:50a48036010a0fabf90b59e32502dcb61e18cb01e4915db0a5910ec69da9952f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3ab980e3580e6939aedbd4dd27b871ec3fa92574faaa38f471ef4211c86db034", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nBefore stating and proving\nProposition <REF_0001>\nin its correct generality we briefly state and prove it for\nclosed immersions. Namely, some of the preceding arguments\nare quite a bit easier to follow in the case of a closed immersion and\nso we repeat them here in their simplified form.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nIn the rest of this section <MATH_0001> is a closed immersion.\nThe functor\n<MATH_0002>\nwill be denoted <MATH_0003> as indicated. Since being a closed immersion\nis preserved under arbitrary base change the scheme <MATH_0004> is a closed subscheme\nof <MATH_0005>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:188780ca0d268b3c6f81988c4710354845afe0b1e9da076c4fb2b54b04707544", "unit_id": "tag:04E1:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04E1", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$U, U'$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$h : U_Z \\to U'_Z$", "MATH_0005": "$Z$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nU & W \\ar[l]_a \\ar[r]^b & U'\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0008": "$a_Z : W_Z \\to U_Z$", "MATH_0009": "$h = b_Z \\circ (a_Z)^{-1}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-closed-immersion-almost-full}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:74e09e671723680a111dbdc8165172f020db28794c274a8fcacc1bf7539e6a72", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5078a3b50dae8869f65a7ceffe1f5e6d12d119b6889e1a81acfc3aad17b7c44d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a closed immersion of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be schemes <ACCENT_0001>tale over <MATH_0003>. Let <MATH_0004>\nbe a morphism over <MATH_0005>. Then there exists a diagram\n<MATH_0006>\nin <MATH_0007> such that <MATH_0008>\nis an isomorphism and <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:293e7d0d4a53509515356acbe77951625eaf9c2813ca40d3a64b53e651c7441e", "unit_id": "tag:04FV:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04E1", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'E", "MATH_0001": "$M = U \\times_X U'$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Gamma_h \\subset M_Z$", "MATH_0003": "$h$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Gamma_h$", "MATH_0005": "$\\text{pr}_{1, Z} : M_Z \\to U_Z$", "MATH_0006": "$W \\subset M$", "MATH_0007": "$M_Z$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Gamma_h$", "MATH_0009": "$a = \\text{pr}_1|_W$", "MATH_0010": "$b = \\text{pr}_2|_W$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{etale-proposition-properties-sections}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b5d2c45548dbc21cc41dfbf91c4c02fd56c24784ad0588f91161e654f98ae176", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:356a304a7eab54c1b9ea1a8a12ea0409bef926502cecf486e78d3f50106db360", "source_text": "Consider the scheme <MATH_0001>. The graph <MATH_0002>\nof <MATH_0003> is open. This is true for example as <MATH_0004> is the image of a\nsection of the <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism <MATH_0005>, see\n<ACCENT_0002>tale Morphisms, Proposition <REF_0001>.\nHence there exists an open subscheme <MATH_0006> whose intersection with\nthe closed subset <MATH_0007> is <MATH_0008>. Set <MATH_0009>\nand <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9ca2927f9bde7dcbe1e8dfd2a94e8a6c87cea5e6cc7d71bb394a73c372905f97", "unit_id": "tag:04FV:proof"}
